    "background_story": "Solomon was a renowned philosopher and scholar who had spent his entire career studying the works of a prominent thinker. He had written extensively on the subject, and his books were considered the definitive texts on the matter. However, as he delved deeper into his research, Solomon began to uncover disturbing inconsistencies and flaws in the thinker's arguments. Despite the potential backlash, he felt compelled to repudiate the thinker's ideas, which he had once held in such high esteem. In a bold and provocative paper, Solomon laid out his criticisms, sparking a heated debate within the academic community. While some of his colleagues turned against him, Solomon's courage in repudiating the flawed ideas earned him a newfound respect for his intellectual honesty and integrity.",
